  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat age-based allowance rule does Shawna use to calculate her father's weekly allowance? Shawna's father is six times as old as Shawna. The allowance is paid weekly.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Shawna’s age be \\(s\\). Her father’s age is therefore\n\n\\[\n6s.\n\\]\n\nHowever, no specific allowance formula is provided. If the allowance is proportional to age, say\n\n\\[\n\\text{weekly allowance}=k(\\text{age}),\n\\]\n\nthen her father’s allowance would be\n\n\\[\nk(6s)=6ks,\n\\]\n\nwhich is six times Shawna’s allowance.\n\nThus, the only rule that can be determined is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s weekly allowance is six times Shawna’s weekly allowance}}\n\\]\n\nThe actual dollar amount cannot be found without knowing the allowance rate.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Shawna's father is five times as old as Shawna.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Shawna’s age be \\(s\\). Her father’s age is\n\n\\[\n5s.\n\\]\n\nIf Shawna calculates allowances proportionally to age, then her father’s weekly allowance is\n\n\\[\n5\n\\]\n\ntimes Shawna’s weekly allowance.\n\nTherefore, the age-based rule is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s weekly allowance} = 5 \\times \\text{Shawna’s weekly allowance}}\n\\]\n\nAn exact dollar amount cannot be determined without knowing Shawna’s allowance or the rate per year of age.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Shawna is four times as old as Aliya.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Aliya’s age be \\(a\\).\n\n- Shawna is four times as old as Aliya:\n  \\[\n  S=4a\n  \\]\n- Shawna’s father is five times as old as Shawna:\n  \\[\n  F=5S=5(4a)=20a\n  \\]\n\nSo Shawna’s father is **20 times as old as Aliya**.\n\nIf the weekly allowance is proportional to age, then:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s allowance}=5\\times\\text{Shawna’s allowance}=20\\times\\text{Aliya’s allowance}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Shawna is three times as old as Aliya.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Aliya’s age be \\(a\\).\n\n- Shawna is three times as old as Aliya:\n  \\[\n  S=3a\n  \\]\n- Her father is five times as old as Shawna:\n  \\[\n  F=5S=5(3a)=15a\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, Shawna’s father is **15 times as old as Aliya**. If the allowance is proportional to age, the rule is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s allowance}=5\\times\\text{Shawna’s allowance}=15\\times\\text{Aliya’s allowance}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Aliya is 3 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old.\n\n- Shawna is three times Aliya’s age:\n  \\[\n  3 \\times 3=9\n  \\]\n  So Shawna is \\(9\\).\n- Shawna’s father is five times Shawna’s age:\n  \\[\n  5 \\times 9=45\n  \\]\n  So her father is \\(45\\).\n\nThus, the age-based allowance rule is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s weekly allowance}=45\\text{ times the allowance per year of age}}\n\\]\n\nFor example, if Shawna gives \\( \\$1\\) per year of age, her father receives \\(\\boxed{\\$45\\text{ per week}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Shawna gives her father an allowance equal to 2 dollars for each year of his age.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old, so Shawna is\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 3=9\n\\]\n\nyears old. Her father is\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 9=45\n\\]\n\nyears old.\n\nShawna gives him \\(\\$2\\) for each year of his age:\n\n\\[\n45 \\times \\$2=\\$90.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, his weekly allowance is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$90\\text{ per week}}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How old is Shawna's father?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old, and Shawna is three times as old:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 3=9\n\\]\n\nShawna is \\(9\\) years old. Her father is five times as old as Shawna:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 9=45\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Shawna’s father is 45 years old.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
